<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="<%= ui_theme %>">
  <head>
    <%= render "layouts/head" %>
  </head>

  <%# `shell` (shell_controller.js) on the signed-in body only: the search shortcuts and the column's
      sheet below 960px. Turbo swaps the body on every visit, so it reconnects with each page. %>
  <%= tag.body class: body_classes, data: ({ controller: "shell" } if shell_signed_in?) do %>
    <%# THE FIRST ELEMENT IN BODY ON BOTH BRANCHES: a keyboard user's first Tab lands here and jumps
        past the strip and the left column to main#main, which both main elements below carry
        (skip_link_test.rb). Hidden above the viewport until focused; positioned absolutely, so it
        never takes a place in the shell's layout (components.css). %>
    <a href="#main" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a>
    <%# `shell_signed_in?`, not `user_signed_in?` — a PUBLIC page (Public::BaseController, stage 3,
        S3-4) renders the visitor's shell even for its signed-in owner, because what a maker wants
        from their own public URL is an honest preview of what a visitor sees. %>
    <% if shell_signed_in? %>
      <%# THE LEFT COLUMN IS A SLOT (Shop manual spec §7): a page supplies its own with
          `content_for :column`, and otherwise its section's default renders
          (layouts/column/_<name>, ShellHelper::COLUMNS). Rendered BEFORE the strip so the strip's
          Contents button knows whether there is a column to open; drawn after it. A section with
          none (Search) gets no column, and main takes the width. %>
      <% column = content_for?(:column) ? content_for(:column) : render("layouts/column") %>
      <%= render "layouts/strip", column: column.present? %>
      <%= tag.div class: class_names("shell-body", "shell-body--column": column.present?) do %>
        <% if column.present? %>
          <%# A LANDMARK, NOT A SECOND MAIN NAV: the strip's four places are "Main"; this lists what
              is inside the lit one. Below 960px it is the sheet the strip's Contents button opens
              (shell_controller.js), and the scrim after it closes it. %>
          <aside class="column" id="column" aria-label="Contents" data-shell-target="column"
                 data-action="keydown.esc->shell#closeColumn">
            <%= column %>
          </aside>
          <div class="column-scrim" data-action="click->shell#closeColumn" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <% end %>
        <div class="shell-main">
          <%= render "layouts/flash" %>
          <%# Pages that need the full width opt in with content_for :container_class, "container-wide"
              (the addon host page does, from its manifest). Inert everywhere else.

              fileopen_controller.js is mounted ONCE, here, so every file link on a signed-in page can
              opt in through FilesHelper#file_open_data (a click opens the file, a double-click opens
              it in a new tab). The visitor's main below has none: public pages are out of scope
              (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-file-click-and-model-page-design.md). %>
          <main id="main" class="container <%= content_for(:container_class) %>" data-controller="fileopen">
            <%# Renders nothing unless this request's port call failed (the partial decides). Signed-in
                only: a visitor is never told about the owner's storage, and a Public:: controller
                has no `capabilities` helper to name a cause with. %>
            <%= render "layouts/library_unreachable" %>
            <%= render "layouts/demo_banner" %>
            <%# THE PAGE HEAD'S CAPS PATH (spec §7; design-system.md rule 9): the page's breadcrumb
                through `content_for :crumbs`, or its title when it supplies none. It left the top
                bar for the head of the page, and it carries no control. %>
            <div class="page-path">
              <% if content_for?(:crumbs) %>
                <%= content_for(:crumbs) %>
              <% else %>
                <span class="page-path-title"><%= page_title_text %></span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
            <%= yield %>
          </main>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <%= render "layouts/tabbar" %>
      <%# THE CALCULATOR MODAL, once per signed-in page and closed until something carrying
          `data-calculator-open` opens it (layouts/_calculator.html.erb). Last in the shell, so its
          dialog is never the first Tab stop. %>
      <%= render "layouts/calculator" %>
    <% else %>
      <%# STAGE 4, S4-5: THE VISITOR'S ONLY CHROME, ON A PUBLIC SURFACE ALONE. Devise's pages share
          this branch and must not get a site nav under their sign-in card, which is what the guard
          says — and `public_shell?` is the same question `shell_signed_in?` asked one line up. %>
      <%= render "layouts/public_header" if public_shell? %>
      <%= render "layouts/flash" %>
      <%# `auth-main` (a 440px column for the sign-in card) is the DEFAULT here rather than a fixed
          class: a PUBLIC page (stage 3, S3-4) renders on this same anonymous branch and needs the
          full width the signed-in pages get. A page opts out by naming its own container class;
          anything that names none — every Devise page — keeps exactly the auth card's layout. %>
      <main id="main" class="container <%= content_for(:container_class).presence || "auth-main" %>">
        <%= yield %>
      </main>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</html>
